      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You classify the latest Slack message in a thread that already has an open Service Desk escalation.\n\nReturn exactly one label:\nCASE_FOLLOWUP\nor\nNEW_TOPIC\n\nUse CASE_FOLLOWUP when the latest message is about the existing escalation/case, for example:\n- \"any update?\"\n- \"follow up please\"\n- \"no answer yet?\"\n- \"what is the status?\"\n- \"can someone help with this case?\"\n- \"is Barbara there?\"\n\nUse NEW_TOPIC when the latest message asks a separate business-knowledge question that can be handled independently, for example:\n- \"while we wait, what are my leave benefits?\"\n- \"do we have sick leave?\"\n- \"what are our company holidays?\"\n- \"what is the expense policy?\"\n\nDo not answer the user.\nDo not explain your choice.\nReturn only CASE_FOLLOWUP or NEW_TOPIC.\n\nRECENT SLACK THREAD:\n{{ $json.thread_context }}\n\nLATEST USER MESSAGE:\n{{ $json.question }}\n",
        "batching": {}
      },
